Description:
Ragdoll Brainrot Meme: Walk Challenge! is a casual puzzle game with ragdoll physics, long legs, meme characters, a walking challenge, and crash scenes!

Game Features:
🕺 Long-legs challenge;
🧠 Meme brainrot chaos;
🕹️ Easy controls;
🏆 Levels of varying difficulty;
💥 Ragdoll physics;

Want to test your nerves, logic, and balance? Get ready — here, every step might be your last!

Instructions:
1. Hold and stretch the character’s legs;
2. Release and watch your long-legged hero take a step;
3. Overcome obstacles and don’t fall flat on your face;
4. Go as far as you can and show who’s the real walking master.

Choose one of the three game modes:
-"Puzzles" - solving spatial puzzles with a limited number of tiles;
- "Board Clearing" - clearing the board from mahjong tiles in limited time;
- "Arcade" - is an endless mode with increasing difficulty, where you need to combine mahjong tiles on the board for as long as possible, without allowing them to be too much.

COMPUTER INPUTS:
- LEFT MOUSE BUTTON - drop the tile on the board;
- "R" - restart current level;
- "H" - show hint for current puzzle;
- "ESC" - open and close the pause menu.

MOBILE INPUTS:
- All controls are performed by TAPPING and/or MOVING YOUR FINGER across the screen.

Simple and intuitive gameplay - drag and drop items and connect them at the bottom of the screen.

- Match two identical items at the bottom of the screen to create a match;
- Connect all the items to complete the level;
- Unlock new items, avatars, and skins by completing more levels!

There are three types of magical abilities:
- create new pawn;
- create new obstacle;
- change one piece to another.

To use the ability, drag the card onto an empty cell (if it is a new pawn or a new obstacle) or onto a piece (if it is a change of piece).

The goal of Sudoku is to fill the 9x9 playing field (each row, column and 3x3 block) with numbers from 1 to 9. The basic rules of Sudoku are:
- vertical numbers should not be repeated;
- numbers should not be duplicated horizontally;
- a number can appear in a 3x3 square only once.

- Tap on 2 or more connected blocks of the same color to pop them;
- The more blocks you pop at once, the higher your score;
- Clear the entire board for bonus points;
- Plan your moves to finish levels with the fewest taps;
- Use smart strategies and boosters to beat challenging levels!
